[{:db/id "q-87461/selection/abe476e447976564bc5c670fe73789666287b967d49bbed12b1d85144449e63e" :answer/id #uuid "f4e84b46-9162-50e2-9572-94c6732c0ba3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "23" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-87461/selection/a4c8bdda186d0d425e9963bf17967cd5e356d934f319fa58135b8f8cf8a589f8" :answer/id #uuid "9fd36aab-53a6-5e41-a336-656695904932" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "30" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-87461/selection/e471e527b99fc0fbfae8bbb79ef8dabdc0f182c810d39e905ffd5c0a5ed28ffa" :answer/id #uuid "2caf0726-cc42-5498-a770-2e8181eef8c5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{175}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-87461/selection/f99ffb0cf114d638f01270deb78ab7e5b7d192d79c6b066fb9f8bf3e1ab3436a" :answer/id #uuid "050ecf80-caa5-5a1e-98b3-1fe6e027472d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{79}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-87461/selection/15092e022b59bb714d9ac4eb632cc1416f135045576aa341fe1e14a460caee64" :answer/id #uuid "c7512ef5-0eeb-585c-b07a-079ddbe0d77f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{88}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-87461/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5c264da9-64ee-541a-a69f-ac10499f855b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-87461/selection/15092e022b59bb714d9ac4eb632cc1416f135045576aa341fe1e14a460caee64" :answer-field/choices ["q-87461/selection/abe476e447976564bc5c670fe73789666287b967d49bbed12b1d85144449e63e" "q-87461/selection/a4c8bdda186d0d425e9963bf17967cd5e356d934f319fa58135b8f8cf8a589f8" "q-87461/selection/e471e527b99fc0fbfae8bbb79ef8dabdc0f182c810d39e905ffd5c0a5ed28ffa" "q-87461/selection/f99ffb0cf114d638f01270deb78ab7e5b7d192d79c6b066fb9f8bf3e1ab3436a" "q-87461/selection/15092e022b59bb714d9ac4eb632cc1416f135045576aa341fe1e14a460caee64"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-87461" :question/id #uuid "43a803fe-7810-57d7-ba47-44721a266a52" :question/math-academy-id "q-87461" :question/is-example false :question/problem "What is the variance of the following data set?\n\n$$\n3,\\,1,\\,15,\\,3,\\,2,\\,12\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If we have a data set that consists of the points ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n},$ then the variance of the data set is given by \n\n$$\n{\\sigma }^{2}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}$ is the mean of the data set.\n\nFirst, we need to compute the mean. There are $n=6$ points in our data set, so the mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot (3+1+15+3+2+12) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot 36 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[(3-6)^{2}+(1-6)^{2}+(15-6)^{2}+(3-6)^{2}+(2-6)^{2}+(12-6)^{2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[9+25+81+9+16+36] \\\\  & =\\frac{176}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{88}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-87461/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b6b41a05-7b11-52b8-a407-af505dffaf10"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-87461"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-246716/field-1/e22421c390ac579ee16b3e84dedae9210c741cce3e7de3d384c2e7110b82bf83" :answer/id #uuid "b88a22f6-1ed9-5c79-9092-1fd04da68a94" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{43}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-246716/field-1/dc3a27f43bf0a726d88091efea3e3d1598b3ee59363a2c4b56cb4cfadf8c4da5" :answer/id #uuid "2048d606-0888-5c13-bb07-acf4b1bb54fa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{43}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-246716/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "2d6fa9e8-9866-5d83-8c96-da376ae8a15f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-246716/field-1/e22421c390ac579ee16b3e84dedae9210c741cce3e7de3d384c2e7110b82bf83" :answer-field/choices ["q-246716/field-1/e22421c390ac579ee16b3e84dedae9210c741cce3e7de3d384c2e7110b82bf83" "q-246716/field-1/dc3a27f43bf0a726d88091efea3e3d1598b3ee59363a2c4b56cb4cfadf8c4da5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-246716" :question/id #uuid "d2a3b06a-d69e-536d-b805-8142d5ea37d0" :question/math-academy-id "q-246716" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Compute the variance ${\\sigma }^{2}$ of the following data set:\n\n$$\n10,\\,23,\\,17,\\,18\n$$\n\n${\\sigma }^{2}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If we have a data set that consists of the points ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n},$ then the variance of the data set is given by \n\n$$\n{\\sigma }^{2}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}$ is the mean of the data set.\n\nFirst, we need to compute the mean. There are $n=4$ points in our data set, so the mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (10+23+17+18) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 68 \\\\  & =17.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(10-17)^{2}+(23-17)^{2}+(17-17)^{2}+(18-17)^{2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[49+36+0+1] \\\\  & =\\frac{86}{4} \\\\  & =21.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-246716/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b6b41a05-7b11-52b8-a407-af505dffaf10"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-246716"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-263297/field-1/c8390e6e47f204804be1b119707a8dc26369a7150f324fa96f6c78cd41c41fd3" :answer/id #uuid "34ab0069-2ae3-52dd-81ec-da5f8966e2db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{65}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-263297/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "31c0de7c-d4c0-50e9-a691-f4cd8a9872cb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-263297/field-1/c8390e6e47f204804be1b119707a8dc26369a7150f324fa96f6c78cd41c41fd3" :answer-field/choices ["q-263297/field-1/c8390e6e47f204804be1b119707a8dc26369a7150f324fa96f6c78cd41c41fd3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-263297" :question/id #uuid "c83c3ac2-cbf3-5dd1-9b5c-3ade2eb7f446" :question/math-academy-id "q-263297" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Compute the variance ${\\sigma }^{2}$ of the following data set:\n\n$$\n1,\\,-6,\\,-1,\\,3,\\,-11,\\,-4\n$$\n\nDo not round your answer.\n\n${\\sigma }^{2}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If we have a data set that consists of the points ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n},$ then the variance of the data set is given by \n\n$$\n{\\sigma }^{2}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}$ is the mean of the data set.\n\nFirst, we need to compute the mean. There are $n=6$ points in our data set, so the mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot (1-6-1+3-11-4) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot (-18) \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[(1-(-3))^{2}+(-6-(-3))^{2}+(-1-(-3))^{2}+(3-(-3))^{2}+(-11-(-3))^{2}+(-4-(-3))^{2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[16+9+4+36+64+1] \\\\  & =\\frac{130}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{65}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-263297/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b6b41a05-7b11-52b8-a407-af505dffaf10"