swer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-87464" :question/id #uuid "8bf3e409-e4bf-5587-9c98-135a36520a77" :question/math-academy-id "q-87464" :question/is-example false :question/problem "What is the variance of the following data set?\n\n$$\n-3,\\,1,\\,-5,\\,-5,\\,2,\\,-8\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If we have a data set that consists of the points ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n},$ then the variance of the data set is given by \n\n$$\n{\\sigma }^{2}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}$ is the mean of the data set.\n\nFirst, we need to compute the mean. There are $n=6$ points in our data set, so the mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot (-3+1-5-5+2-8) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot (-18) \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[(-3-(-3))^{2}+(1-(-3))^{2}+(-5-(-3))^{2}+(-5-(-3))^{2}+(2-(-3))^{2}+(-8-(-3))^{2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[0+16+4+4+25+25] \\\\  & =\\frac{74}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{37}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-87464/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b6b41a05-7b11-52b8-a407-af505dffaf10"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-87464"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-263258/field-1/4c919dd28b6dc49158e4bc0cd4ecb2267c6fa1a0cbd5673af1ca376ab1c8a23e" :answer/id #uuid "f26b5147-ea3f-5baa-88a7-47a9b0cba9eb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-263258/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "69ecaea7-9779-515a-acc2-c3ebff64699e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-263258/field-1/4c919dd28b6dc49158e4bc0cd4ecb2267c6fa1a0cbd5673af1ca376ab1c8a23e" :answer-field/choices ["q-263258/field-1/4c919dd28b6dc49158e4bc0cd4ecb2267c6fa1a0cbd5673af1ca376ab1c8a23e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-263258" :question/id #uuid "bbd753fe-03e2-53a5-a2b0-e6fa1fba36c6" :question/math-academy-id "q-263258" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Compute the variance ${\\sigma }^{2}$ of the following data set:\n\n$$\n14,\\,21,\\,13,\\,16\n$$\n\n${\\sigma }^{2}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If we have a data set that consists of the points ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n},$ then the variance of the data set is given by \n\n$$\n{\\sigma }^{2}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}$ is the mean of the data set.\n\nFirst, we need to compute the mean. There are $n=4$ points in our data set, so the mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (14+21+13+16) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 64 \\\\  & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(14-16)^{2}+(21-16)^{2}+(13-16)^{2}+(16-16)^{2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[4+25+9+0] \\\\  & =\\frac{38}{4} \\\\  & =9.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-263258/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b6b41a05-7b11-52b8-a407-af505dffaf10"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-263258"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-87253/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "9e5ef32c-f74f-5ae7-a413-9df0612f59cd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-87253/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" :answer/id #uuid "6a057ea2-aeac-5e64-bc9f-9dfc22b4b1c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-87253/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "04333eeb-be88-5ac4-ad88-f0772250a59b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-87253/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "c20c13d6-924e-5e4e-bede-b09ec5d56fe0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-87253/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "de1cd017-4414-5328-99e7-7a79015861be" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-87253/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9ba88001-261a-508d-b1d7-ee26d2fbef9f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-87253/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-87253/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-87253/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" "q-87253/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-87253/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" "q-87253/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-87253" :question/id #uuid "97b5a09c-ba97-5deb-97d8-4bd8abb87bfa" :question/math-academy-id "q-87253" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Compute the variance ${\\sigma }^{2}$ of a data set ${x}_{i}$ consisting of $15$ data points, where \n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{x}_{i}=-30,\\,{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{x}_{i}^{2}=120.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If we have a data set that consists of the points ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n},$ then the variance can be computed as\n\n$$\n{\\sigma }^{2}=\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-(\\overset{―}{x})^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}$ is the mean of the data set and $\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}$ is the mean of the squares of the points in the data set.\n\nFirst, let's compute $\\overset{―}{x}.$ There are $n=15$ points in our data set, and we know that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{x}_{i}=-30,$ so we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{15}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{15}\\cdot (-30) \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute $\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}.$ We know that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{x}_{i}^{2}=120,$ so we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{15}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{x}_{i}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{15}\\cdot 120 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2} & =\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-(\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & =8-{(-2)}^{2} \\\\  & =8-4 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-87253/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7eab4249-544e-56c6-81c0-e6db84033701"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-87253"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-263335/field-1/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer/id #uuid "df0be136-e51e-5720-b004-f890a3a69cf5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-263335/field-1/12b7d840a997b0af25896f37c76d366155c72a970c1525c62ec119b69786f393" :answer/id #uuid "fd31c25e-af56-5f49-a037-0cd3da7f69a5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "13" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-263335/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "17c4ca46-cb0e-59e0-b93f-0a4c160d669b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-263335/field-1/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer-field/choices ["q-263335/field-1/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" "q-263335/field-1/12b7d840a997b0af25896f37c76d366155c72a970c1525c62ec119b69786f393"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-263335" :question/id #uuid "d71b5626-730b-55f2-b59e-5134ae2d2058" :question/math-academy-id "q-263335" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Compute the variance ${\\sigma }^{2}$ of a data set ${x}_{i}$ consisting of $8$ data points, where\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{x}_{i}=104,\\,{\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{x}_{i}^{2}=1448.\n$$\n\n${\\sigma }^{2}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If we have a data set that consists of the points ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n},$ then the variance can be computed as\n\n$$\n{\\sigma }^{2}=\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-(\\overset{―}{x})^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}$ is the mean of the data set and $\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}$ is the mean of the squares of the points in the data set.\n\nFirst, let's compute $\\overset{―}{x}.$ There are $n=8$ points in our data set, and we know that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{x}_{i}=104,$ so we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\cdot (104) \\\\  & =13.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute $\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}.$ We know that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{x}_{i}^{2}=1448,$ so we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{x}_{i}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\cdot 1448 \\\\  & =181.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2} & =\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-(\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & =181-{(13)}^{2} \\\\  & =181-169 \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-263335/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7eab4249-544e-56c6-81c0-e6db84033701"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-263335"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-87603/selection/dc3a27f43bf0a726d88091efea3e3d1598b3ee59363a2c4b56cb4cfadf8c4da5" :answer/id #uuid "41f41b40-94bd-5a8d-9c68-9c73965dddfc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{43}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-87603/selection/c266f84c876fcde2390cc8404b7ae74cbe3f14d3c2d1a0a0f23d8443afff0222" :answer/id #uuid "512397ed-691d-50ee-b8c4-103d47f28e97" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{51}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-87603/selection/a332dea2328e7f7920dc78199b51c5206506c65a9828c8335bb4addd70724a24" :answer/id #uuid "e1102d5e-1b15-5722-b01b-e54ca95ad5fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{44}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-87603/selection/cfb90d5c6d9365297771354cc52aeb1795f8ac24ce659170baf9a125d3220276" :answer/id #uuid "177fb8b7-581b-5c38-bb0f-c6f75c112a42" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{35}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-87603/selection/4ca7e04cb32d17c1971e27f96c827d785e809ee86fbe2e04813f39f29bdc8cde" :answer/id #uuid "664bcbe0-72a0-54f5-a7b9-61ab654fbded" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{25}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-87603/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "fadf5811-c1c9-5e96-9ca8-d1c216556f64" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-87603/selection/cfb90d5c6d9365297771354cc52aeb1795f8ac24ce659170baf9a125d3220276" :answer-field/choices ["q-87603/selection/dc3a27f43bf0a726d88091efea3e3d1598b3ee59363a2c4b56cb4cfadf8c4da5" "q-87603/selection/c266f84c876fcde2390cc8404b7ae74cbe3f14d3c2d1a0a0f23d8443afff0222" "q-87603/selection/a332dea2328e7f7920dc78199b51c5206506c65a9828c8335bb4addd70724a24" "q-87603/selection/cfb90d5c6d9365297771354cc52aeb1795f8ac24ce659170baf9a125d3220276" "q-87603/selection/4ca7e04cb32d17c1971e27f96c827d785e809ee86fbe2e04813f39f29bdc8cde"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-87603" :question/id #uuid "de0bbf5f-f549-5d46-99ea-43143f517a2d" :question/math-academy-id "q-87603" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Compute the variance ${\\sigma }^{2}$ of a data set ${x}_{i}$ consisting of $12$ data points, where \n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{12}{x}_{i}=-60,\\,{\\sum }_{i=1}^{12}{x}_{i}^{2}=440.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If we have a data set that consists of the points ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n},$ then the variance can be computed as\n\n$$\n{\\sigma }^{2}=\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-(\\overset{―}{x})^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}$ is the mean of the data set and $\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}$ is the mean of the squares of the points in the data set.\n\nFirst, let's compute $\\overset{―}{x}.$ There are $n=12$ points in our data set, and we know that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{12}{x}_{i}=-60,$ so we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{12}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}\\cdot (-60) \\\\  & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute $\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}.$ We know that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{12}{x}_{i}^{2}=440,$ so we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{12}{x}_{i}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}\\cdot 440 \\\\  & =\\frac{440}{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{110}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2} & =\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-(\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{110}{3}-{(-5)}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{110}{3}-25 \\\\  & =\\frac{110-75}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{35}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-87603/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7eab4249-544e-56c6-81c0-e6db84033701"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-87603"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/valida