{1}{5}\\cdot 170 \\\\  & =34.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2} & =\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-(\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & =34-{(-4)}^{2} \\\\  & =34-16 \\\\  & =18.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-87608/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0040fc1-2134-5eaa-a3e8-6c7a457f75f5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-87608"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-246721/field-1/a7c6d204c00c870aecb7a4bd25dac1f3049948d7743b19cc024a81625d2ebcb0" :answer/id #uuid "9863e07b-2506-50ab-a86b-7acfbcddaba7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{37}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-246721/field-1/2a8d412c59e79313e9b70dc74e940c9f4cf0ba48e4f7778fd6de55eed4914b18" :answer/id #uuid "5175476a-fa2a-574d-8778-e574709d52cf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{74}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-246721/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "d71e666a-672d-51fa-8c3d-eb2e0b29bc90" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-246721/field-1/a7c6d204c00c870aecb7a4bd25dac1f3049948d7743b19cc024a81625d2ebcb0" :answer-field/choices ["q-246721/field-1/a7c6d204c00c870aecb7a4bd25dac1f3049948d7743b19cc024a81625d2ebcb0" "q-246721/field-1/2a8d412c59e79313e9b70dc74e940c9f4cf0ba48e4f7778fd6de55eed4914b18"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-246721" :question/id #uuid "0d4f682c-c60d-5829-8c4d-e7ed9d401f55" :question/math-academy-id "q-246721" :question/is-example false :question/problem "What is the variance of the following data set?\n\n$$\n12,\\,15,\\,15,\\,17,\\,21,\\,22\n$$\n\nDo not round your answer.\n\n${\\sigma }^{2}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If we have a data set that consists of the points ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n},$ then the variance can be computed as\n\n$$\n{\\sigma }^{2}=\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-(\\overset{―}{x})^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}$ is the mean of the data set and $\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}$ is the mean of the squares of the points in the data set.\n\nFirst, let's compute $\\overset{―}{x}.$ There are $n=6$ points in our data set, so the mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot (12+15+15+17+21+22) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot 102 \\\\  & =17.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute $\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}.$ Computing the mean of the squares of the points in the data set, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot ({12}^{2}+{15}^{2}+{15}^{2}+{17}^{2}+{21}^{2}+{22}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot (144+225+225+289+441+484) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot 1808 \\\\  & =\\frac{1808}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{904}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2} & =\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-(\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{904}{3}-{(17)}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{904}{3}-289 \\\\  & =\\frac{904-867}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{37}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-246721/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0040fc1-2134-5eaa-a3e8-6c7a457f75f5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-246721"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-87610/selection/c9ec5d6cdf4e67c7f8bce68475bed400e56bf403f3d09b5928f78b6baa512eab" :answer/id #uuid "7c218d9c-fa83-56c5-8192-9ed2e4a48037" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "27" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-87610/selection/abe476e447976564bc5c670fe73789666287b967d49bbed12b1d85144449e63e" :answer/id #uuid "de475755-78d3-51eb-9d9d-35d900721c4d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "23" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-87610/selection/a38ef12f135c1e6010d68ed21f81bc27372a73a756455b7066f6182c46018cc8" :answer/id #uuid "392ab0a5-8a6d