d8" "q-87615/selection/da78c566f548e0d87feab5831927ec39b3df2dd2077262d9a307b007c13d64d5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-87615" :question/id #uuid "f9294266-cc49-5b09-ab07-a7b115d05d2a" :question/math-academy-id "q-87615" :question/is-example false :question/problem "What is the standard deviation of the following data set?\n\n$$\n-7,\\,3,\\,-5,\\,-1,\\,-5\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The standard deviation of a data set ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ is the square root of the variance:\n\n$$\n\\sigma =\\sqrt{{\\sigma }^{2}}=\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})^{2}}=\\sqrt{\\,\\,\\,\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-{(\\overset{―}{x})}^{2}}\n$$\n\nFirst, let's compute $\\overset{―}{x}.$ There are $n=5$ points in our data set, so the mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot (-7+3-5-1-5) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot (-15) \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute $\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}.$ Computing the mean of the squares of the points in the data set, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot [(-7)^{2}+{3}^{2}+(-5)^{2}+(-1)^{2}+(-5)^{2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot [49+9+25+1+25] \\\\  & =\\frac{109}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2} & =\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-(\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{109}{5}-{(-3)}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{109}{5}-9 \\\\  & =\\frac{109-45}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{64}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the standard deviation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sigma  & =\\sqrt{{\\sigma }^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{64}{5}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8\\sqrt{5}}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-87615/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a72dae6-2bbf-5e59-b71d-8ee57f589753"] :knowledge-po